/* src/coop-test/test_main.cpp - THE OFFLINE SUITE (P7u, design-offline-tests).
 *
 * It runs as STEP 0 of src\coop-plugin\build.bat: a non-zero exit fails the build BEFORE the DLL is linked, so
 * a DLL carrying a failed assertion cannot reach tools\deploy.ps1. The suite is not advisory.
 *
 * WHAT IT CAN AND CANNOT SAY. Every test here is arithmetic, format or ordering over src\common\clockmath.cpp,
 * which reads no engine memory. A passing suite says NOTHING about the engine (design-offline-tests 7.4); what
 * it does say is that review-p7j H-1's post-condition - the throttle can never write a lower time - holds over
 * a swept grid rather than in a comment.
 *
 * A FAILURE PRINTS THE INPUTS IT READ, not only the answer it computed (6a lesson 12). Every input below is a
 * literal: no test's precondition is computed by the function it is checking (design-offline-tests 7.5).
 *
 * C++03 (VS2010 v100): no auto, no nullptr, no range-for.
 *
 * ONE OF SEVERAL FILES (owner decision 1204). Older, settled tests sit in suite_part1.cpp .. suite_part7.cpp so that
 * cl /MP8 compiles the suite's files side by side; suite.h carries what the files share. This file keeps the
 * runner, the table (kTests: the run order) and the newer tests. New tests go here.
 */
